Yes, it is possible (I think the names are 'ELF' and 'GNU'); but at least on
some archs I understand the default value for ld is now set to 'gnu' rather
than 'both', and I guess on etch it was 'elf'.  I have no idea why it was
decided not to have a transitional period when oldstable's binutils could
read the objects created by stable's binutils; perhaps object size was a
concern.

