On 5/18/07, Roman Rupp <roman@rupp-center-net.de> wrote:
> -----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
> Hash: SHA1
>
> Hi,
>
> Falko Schmidt schrieb:
> > I've experienced the same issue on a PWS600. Upgrading to version
> > 0.8.0 from unstable fixed it though.
> Hmm, i'm a newbie in these things... How do you installed this newer
> version of thunar with aptitude. I've googled about it and found some
> threads about apt-pinning, but i think i've made some mistakes here and
> aptitude don't show me the newer version. Can you tell me how it works?

First you'll need to add an unstable repository to your
/etc/apt/sources.list e.g:

"deb http://ftp.de.debian.org/debian/ unstable main"

Then update the package lists:

# apt-get update

Now simply install thunar:

# apt-get install -tunstable thunar

Afterwards you can remove the unstable repository from
/etc/apt/sources.list if you don't need it anymore.
As far as I remember I also needed to upgrade some xfce4 libs to get
thunar from unstable work in stable.

Regards,

Falko

